{
  format: 1
  name: pack-unknown-axis-invalid
  suite: static
  spec: ["#modules", "§13.16"]
  note: '''
    §13.16 gives `pack` exactly three axes — `model`, `data`, `history` — each
    addressing "its own coordinate on the timeline". The attack is an axis the
    operator does not define, spelled to look plausible (`snapshot`). If the
    unknown member were dropped, the package would load, the call would return a
    blob, and the author would believe they had extracted a snapshot they never
    asked the engine for and never received. Since a wrong module extract ships
    looking correct, the unknown axis is a LOAD error, not a silent drop.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.modvalue.badaxis@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      companies: {
        $key: "id"
        id: "text"
        modules: { $modules: {} }
      }
      $mut: {
        "archive({ at: module, when: timestamp })": [
          "b = pack(@at, { snapshot: @when })"
          "return { kept: true }"
        ]
      }
    }
    $data: { companies: { acme: {} } }
  }

  expect: { outcome: invalid, violates: ["§13.16"] }
}
